.next/
out/
build
dist


# Debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# TLS material the deploy job writes onto the production box. `secrets/caddy/`
# holds the Cloudflare Origin Certificate and its PRIVATE KEY; `*.pem` above
# already catches the certificate, but not the .key, and a whole-directory rule
# is the one that survives someone adding a third file.
secrets/

# direnv - local only, never commit (may contain secrets)
.envrc
.direnv/

# Visual-check output. Screenshots are evidence for the task you are on, not
# artifacts of the repo — they go stale the moment the UI changes and reviewing
# a binary diff proves nothing.
.visual/

# The Playwright storage state produced by `npm run visual:login`. It holds a
# live JWT for a real account. `.playwright/cli.config.json` IS versioned (it is
# the capture contract); the session never is.
.playwright/auth.json

# Ad-hoc visual scenarios are scratch for one task. A scenario worth keeping
# gets un-ignored by name, right here, next to the reference one.
scripts/visual/scenarios/*.scenario.mjs
!scripts/visual/scenarios/public-profile.scenario.mjs
# The i18n check is not scratch: it is the only thing that proves the three
# locales still render, and the `i18n` skill points at it by name.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/i18n-locales.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the tabs toggle: every other check of "simple mode" is a unit test
# rendering ProfileBlocks with a prop. This is the only one that proves the flag
# survives the database, the API response and the schema parse on its way to a
# logged-out stranger — which is the whole point of the feature.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/profile-tabs-toggle.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the mobile header. Its unit tests can assert the CLASSES on the
# hamburger and the switch, but jsdom has no layout and no stylesheet: only a
# real browser can say the hamburger computes to zero border and the bar's ink
# in both themes, and only a real browser can measure whether "Mudar para o
# tema escuro" still fits beside the knob at 320px. That measurement is what
# fixes the knob's gutter at 40px, so it needs to fail if anyone widens it.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/mobile-header.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the availability check: the component tests assert the STRING each of
# the five states renders, which is the one thing a missing `dark:` variant does
# not change. This is the only proof that all six states are legible in both
# themes, and that the status line holds its height so an arriving verdict
# cannot shove the field out from under the cursor.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/dashboard-username-availability.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the legacy redirect: `router.test.tsx` stubs every page component, so
# it proves the URL resolves and nothing about what the visitor then sees. This
# is the only check that the profile actually RENDERS behind the redirect —
# which is exactly the failure that started this (a link that resolved, to a
# "profile not found").
!scripts/visual/scenarios/legacy-profile-redirect.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the banner/background one. It carries the only paint-proofs in the
# repo: the same patch of card photographed with two DIFFERENT background
# images, and a hit test over the live preview while the veil slider is used.
# Every DOM assertion said the background was fine while it was painted
# underneath an opaque wrapper and invisible to every human — `isVisible()`
# cannot see that class of bug, and neither can a class assertion see a preview
# that another element is painting over.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/banner-background-position.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the dialog chrome. The Dialog's unit tests can assert the DOM
# relationship — X in the header row, header before the scroller — but jsdom has
# no layout, so it cannot say the button ends ABOVE the scroll area, and it
# cannot know where a 15px classic scrollbar would be drawn. That measurement is
# the whole reported bug (the X sitting on the scrollbar's top arrow), and it
# needs to fail if anyone floats the button back over the body. It also carries
# the only proof that the appearance preview's avatar is not painted over by the
# cover strip — a paint-order defect no DOM assertion can see.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/dialog-chrome.scenario.mjs
# Nor is the MinIO upload. Two test files cover the halves — the HTTP route with
# an in-memory store, and the real bucket with no browser — and neither can
# answer "if I drop a photo on the banner tile, does it appear?". That answer
# spans the file input, the multipart request, the bucket's anonymous-read
# policy and an <img> the browser has to decode; this is the only check that
# walks all four.
!scripts/visual/scenarios/minio-upload.scenario.mjs

# Spec working directories are committed (docs/specs/**) — QA session output is
# not, until it is written up.
docs/qa/sessions/

# QA living docs (docs/qa/, bootstrapped 2026-08-22 per .claude/skills/qa-report) —
# generated views & bulky evidence. Source of truth is docs/qa/scenarios/, bugs/,
# journeys/, charters/, reports/, personas.md, README.md, templates/ — all committed.
docs/qa/state.csv
docs/qa/evidence/

# The nightly loop's runtime state. STATE.json / QUEUE.json / MEMORY.md are the
# loop's memory across processes, and the logs are one JSON blob per iteration —
# all of it is a record of ONE night's run, not of the repo. The durable output
# is committed instead: docs/qa/** and docs/nightly-loop.md.
.nightly/
# `--fresh` archives a finished run to .nightly-<timestamp>/. The pattern above
# does NOT match those, and one iteration committed 23 of those artifact files
# (logs, pids, state) into the branch as a result.
.nightly-*/

# @playwright/test output. `.playwright/cli.config.json` stays versioned (it is
# the visual-check capture contract); nothing generated does.
.playwright/e2e-*.json
.playwright/e2e-results/
.playwright/e2e-html/
.playwright/*.log

# deep-review generates hundreds of artifact files per round.
.deep-review/
